# External Reconnaissance & Enumeration Report

Academic coursework project demonstrating a structured, passive-to-active external
reconnaissance methodology against a single target host, selected via Shodan.

> ⚠️ **Scope & Ethics Note:** This assessment was performed as part of a university
> cybersecurity coursework assignment. All testing was limited to a single,
> publicly Shodan-indexed host, used non-intrusive/read-only techniques only
> (no exploitation, brute-force login, or denial-of-service activity), and was
> scoped strictly to the target host itself — explicitly excluding the parent
> domain and any other sites on shared hosting infrastructure.

## Methodology

1. **Target Profiling** — WHOIS and Netcraft for registrar, nameserver, and hosting context
2. **Subdomain Enumeration** — Subfinder + manual DNS checks, scoped to the target host
3. **Service Enumeration** — Nmap (port/service/version detection, NSE scripting for HTTP, TLS, SSH)
4. **Web Enumeration** — Gobuster directory/file discovery
5. **Intelligence Gathering** — Shodan for externally-indexed services and technologies

## Tools Used

`Nmap` · `Gobuster` · `Subfinder` · `WHOIS` · `Netcraft` · `Shodan` · `dig` / `host`

## Key Findings

- 3 open ports identified: SSH (22), HTTP (80), HTTPS (443)
- Both web ports fronted by Cloudflare, serving a JS bot-challenge to automated clients
- One backend endpoint (`/addtocart.php`) discovered via Gobuster, indicating e-commerce functionality
- No subdomains discovered beyond the target host itself
- Full findings, risk analysis, and remediation recommendations in [`recon_report.pdf`](./recon_report.pdf)

